## Status of `erdos_295` (Open Problem)

The theorem `erdos_295` asks whether

$$\lim_{N \to \infty} \bigl(k(N) - (e-1)N\bigr) = +\infty.$$

**This is an open problem.** It is listed at [erdosproblems.com/295](https://www.erdosproblems.com/295) as open. The `answer(sorry)` placeholder cannot be filled with `true` or `false` because the mathematical community does not know the answer.

What is known:
- $k(N) \sim (e-1)N$ as $N \to \infty$ (the leading term is $(e-1)N$).
- The Erdős-Straus result (the variant below) shows $-C < k(N) - (e-1)N \ll N/\log N$ for some constant $C > 0$.
- The open question is whether the difference $k(N) - (e-1)N$ not only stays bounded below but actually tends to $+\infty$.

**I cannot prove or disprove this.** The correct formalization would leave `erdos_295` as an open conjecture with `answer(sorry)` unfilled.

